---

Why this and not MIT: the goal of making this repository public is free
security scanning (CodeQL, secret scanning, dependency review), and none of
those require a permissive licence — only public visibility. An open-source
licence is a separate, one-way decision: once code ships under MIT that version
is licensed forever and cannot be recalled. Reserving rights keeps the option
open. Replacing this file with a real OSS licence is a one-commit change on the
day that becomes the intent.
